\h Leviticus
\toc1 Leviticus
\toc2 Leviticus
\toc3 Lev.
\mt2 The handbook of
\mt1 Sacred Living
\mt3 commonly known as
\mt1 Leviticus
\is1 Introduction
\ip The Latin word \bk Leviticus\bk* means ‘concerning the Levites’, who were the tribe of workers and priests who God chose to serve him at the altar and in other religious ceremonies. Hebrew readers call this document ‘Vayikrā’ which is the first word in the Hebrew and means ‘And he called’ (Yahweh called Mosheh/Moses). Some European and other translations call it ‘The third book of Mosheh/Moses’.
\ip It's presumed that Mosheh wrote this document down while they were all camped there at Mt. Sinai as mentioned in a few places: 1:1, 4:1, 6:1,24, and of 8:1.
\ip This document focuses on the proper values and behaviour that the Israelis should observe as Yahweh's chosen and sacred people. That involved staying ‘clean’ as per Yahweh's values by carefully following his detailed instructions, and by avoiding wickedness.
\ip Some of the instructions apply particularly to the priests (Aharon's/Aaron's descendants) and to the remainder of their own tribe (the Levites that this document is often named after) who served the priests in their sacred ceremonies.
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 Instructions about offerings and sacrifices \ior 1:1–7:38\ior*
\io1 The dedication of Aharon and his sons as Yahweh's priests \ior 8:1–10:20\ior*
\io1 Instructions about ‘clean’ and ‘unclean’ \ior 11:1–15:33\ior*
\io1 The day for getting right with Yahweh \ior 16:1-34\ior*
\io1 Instructions for living and worshipping as a sacred people \ior 17:1–27:34\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\s1 Procedures for burnt sacrifices
\rem /s1 Sacrifices Burned Whole; The Burnt Offering; Offerings and sacrifices; Procedures for the Burnt Offering
\p
\v 1 Yahweh¦46173 \add ≈summoned¦46168\add* Mosheh¦46171 \add !(Moses¦46171)\add* to¦46174 the¦46175 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦46175 and \add ≈told¦46177 him\add*,
\v 2 “Tell¦46179 the¦46182 \add ≈Israelis¦46183\add* that when¦46184 anyone¦46186 presents¦46189 an offering¦46191 to¦46192 Yahweh¦46192, it must be presented from \add &their\add* \add ?own\add* herd¦46198 or flock¦46201.
\v 3 If¦46207 it's from¦46211 the¦46213 herd¦46213, it must be a¦46214 bull with \add ≈no¦46215 defects¦46215\add*. It must¦46216 be presented¦46216 \add ≈in¦46226 front¦46226 of¦46226\add* the¦46219 entrance¦46219 to the¦46221 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦46221 to \add ≈be acceptable¦46225\add* to¦46226 Yahweh¦46227.
\v 4 \add @The¦46229 owner¦46229\add* must¦46229 place his¦46230 hand¦46230 on¦46231 the¦46232 head¦46232 of¦46232 that offering¦46233 to be burnt¦46233, and¦46234 then it¦46234 will¦46234 be¦46234 accepted¦46234 \add ≈make¦46236 him¦46237 right with Yahweh\add*.
\v 5 Then¦46239 he¦46239 must¦46239 slaughter the \add ≈bull in¦46244 front¦46244\add* of¦46244 Yahweh¦46245, and the¦46247 priests¦46249 (Aharon's¦46248 \add !(Aaron's¦46248)\add* descendants¦46247), must¦46246 present¦46246 the¦46252 blood¦46252 and¦46253 splash¦46253 it all¦46260 around¦46260 the¦46259 altar¦46259 which¦46261 is¦46263 by the¦46263 entrance¦46263 of¦46263 the¦46264 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦46264.
\v 6 Then¦46267 \add @the¦46267 presenter¦46267\add* must¦46267 skin¦46267 the¦46270 \add ≈bull\add* and¦46271 cut¦46271 it¦46272 into¦46273 pieces¦46273,
\v 7 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* the¦46276 priest¦46278 Aharon's¦46277 sons¦46276 must¦46275 put¦46275 fire¦46279 on¦46280 the¦46282 altar¦46282 and¦46283 arrange¦46283 wood¦46284 on¦46285 the¦46287 fire¦46287,
\v 8 and¦46289 then \add *they¦46291\add* must¦46289 arrange¦46289 the¦46294 pieces¦46294 (including the¦46297 head¦46297 and¦46298 the¦46300 fat portions) on¦46301 top of the¦46303 burning¦46307 wood¦46303 on the¦46311 altar¦46311.
\v 9 Then¦46313 \add @the presenter\add* must¦46315 wash¦46315 the innards¦46313 and¦46314 the feet with¦46316 water¦46316, and¦46317 the¦46318 priest¦46318 must \add place it\add* on the¦46322 altar¦46322, \add ≈ensuring that every part is completely burnt¦46323 up\add* as a¦46324 pleasing¦46327 aroma¦46325 for¦46328 Yahweh¦46328.
\p
\v 10 “If¦46331 the offering¦46344 is¦46333 from¦46333 the¦46335 flock¦46335 (i.e., a sheep¦46339 or¦46340 a \add #goat¦46343\add*), then¦46331 it must be a¦46345 healthy male¦46345 that's presented¦46347,
\v 11 and¦46349 then it¦46350 must be slaughtered on the¦46352 northern¦46354 side¦46352 of¦46352 the¦46353 altar¦46353 facing¦46355 Yahweh¦46356, and Aharon's¦46359 sons¦46358, the¦46360 priests¦46360, must¦46357 splash¦46357 its¦46363 blood¦46363 on¦46364 the¦46366 altar¦46366, all¦46367 around¦46367.
\v 12 Then¦46369 \add @the¦46369 presenter¦46369\add* must¦46369 cut¦46369 it¦46370 into¦46371 pieces¦46371 and they must¦46378 arrange¦46378 them¦46380 (including the¦46383 head¦46374 and¦46375 fat portions) on¦46385 top of the¦46387 burning¦46387 wood¦46383 on¦46389 the¦46391 altar¦46391.
\v 13 Then¦46393 \add @the presenter\add* must¦46395 wash¦46395 the¦46393 innards¦46393 and¦46394 the¦46394 feet with¦46396 water¦46396, and¦46397 the¦46398 priest¦46398 must¦46402 \add place it\add* on the¦46403 altar¦46403, \add ≈ensuring that every part is¦46404 completely burnt¦46404 up\add* as a¦46406 pleasing¦46408 aroma¦46407 for¦46409 Yahweh¦46409.
