\c 2
\s1 Procedures for grain offerings
\rem /s1 Procedures for the Grain Offering; The Grain Offering; Grain Offerings
\p
\v 1 “When¦46488 someone¦46488 presents a¦46493 grain¦46493 offering¦46493 to¦46494 Yahweh¦46494, it¦46496 must¦46496 be¦46496 as fine¦46495, wheat flour¦46495 \add ≈mixed with\add* \add olive\add*, and with frankincense¦46503 added to the top of it.
\v 2 It¦46505 must be taken to¦46506 the¦46508 priest¦46522 Aharon's¦46509 sons¦46508 who will¦46511 take it \add from them\add*, then take a¦46511 handful out, being sure to get flour¦46515, oil¦46516, and some frankincense¦46520, and¦46521 \add ≈throw that memorial¦46525 portion onto\add* the¦46526 altar¦46526 to get completely burnt up as a¦46527 pleasing¦46529 aroma¦46528 for¦46530 Yahweh¦46530.
\v 3 Then¦46532 the¦46532 rest¦46532 of¦46533 that grain¦46535 offering¦46535 will be for Aharon¦46536 and¦46537 his¦46537 sons¦46537—it's a¦46538 very sacred part from¦46540 the¦46540 gifts for Yahweh¦46541.
\p
\v 4 “When¦46544 \add %someone¦46545\add* presents something baked as \add &their\add* grain¦46547 offering¦46547, it must be baked¦46548 without leaven: either wheat flour¦46550 mixed¦46553 with¦46554 \add olive\add* oil¦46554 and baked into flat¦46556 buns, or else wheat flour biscuits¦46555 with¦46558 \add olive\add* oil¦46558 \add ≈spread on top\add*.
\v 5 Or if¦46561 your grain¦46563 offering¦46563 is done on¦46564 the¦46566 flat pan, it must be wheat flour¦46568 mixed¦46569 with¦46570 \add olive\add* oil¦46570 \add ≈and made into flat¦46571 biscuits\add*
\v 6 that should then be crumbled¦46574 and¦46577 have oil¦46579 poured¦46577 over them as \add &your¦46580\add* grain¦46580 offering¦46580.
\v 7 Or if¦46584 your grain¦46586 offering¦46586 is \add deep-fried\add* in a¦46587 pot, it¦46591 must¦46591 be¦46591 made¦46591 from wheat flour¦46589 with¦46590 \add olive\add* oil¦46590.
\p
\v 8 “\add Any of the above types of\add* grain¦46596 offering¦46596 to¦46600 Yahweh¦46600 must¦46601 be presented¦46601 to¦46602 the¦46604 priest¦46604, and¦46605 he¦46605 will¦46605 take¦46605 it¦46605 to¦46606 the¦46608 altar¦46608.
\v 9 Then¦46610 he¦46610 must¦46610 \add take a handful\add* as a memorial¦46617 portion to¦46619 the¦46619 altar¦46619 to get completely burnt up¦46610 as a¦46620 pleasing¦46622 aroma¦46621 for¦46623 Yahweh¦46623.
\v 10 Then¦46625 the¦46625 rest¦46625 of¦46626 that grain¦46628 offering¦46628 will be for Aharon¦46629 and¦46630 his¦46630 sons¦46630—it's a¦46631 very sacred part from¦46633 the¦46633 gifts for Yahweh¦46634.
\p
\v 11 “Anything that's¦46639 presented¦46640 to¦46641 Yahweh¦46641 as a grain¦46638 offering¦46638 must not¦46642 be¦46643 made¦46643 with any rising agent, because¦46645 any¦46646 leaven¦46648 or honey¦46651 mustn't be burnt¦46654 as a¦46656 gift to¦46657 Yahweh¦46657.
\v 12 \add ≈Foods containing those\add* can be presented as a¦46659 first-fruits¦46660 offering¦46661, but¦46664 they mustn't \add ≈be burnt\add* on the¦46666 altar¦46666.
\v 13 \add ≈However,\add* every¦46673 grain¦46676 offering¦46676 must¦46678 be salted¦46678—the¦46681 salt¦46681 in the¦46682 grain¦46685 offering¦46689 is a reminder of¦46689 \add *our\add* agreement¦46682, \add ≈so it\add* \add ^must always be present\add*.
\p
\v 14 “\add ≈Finally,\add* if¦46694 you¦46696 want to offer ripe grain as a¦46697 grain¦46697 offering¦46697 to¦46699 Yahweh¦46699, then it must be a young¦46700 ear¦46700 of grain that's been roasted¦46701 over the fire¦46702 and presented¦46705 as a grain¦46707 offering¦46707 of¦46707 your¦46708 first¦46708 ripe grains
\v 15 \add ≈with\add* \add olive\add* oil¦46712 on it and some frankincense¦46715 on top. That \add also becomes\add* a¦46716 grain¦46716 offering¦46716,
\v 16 and the¦46720 priest¦46720 must burn a memorial¦46723 portion from it with some¦46724 of¦46724 the crushed grains¦46724 and¦46725 some¦46725 of¦46725 the oil¦46725 and some of the incense, \add to be burnt\add* to become smoke¦46719 as a¦46730 gift to¦46731 Yahweh¦46731.
\c 3
