\v 11 Then¦46948 the¦46949 priest¦46949 must burn¦46948 them on the¦46950 altar¦46950 as a food¦46951 offering¦46952 made¦46948 to¦46953 Yahweh¦46953 by fire¦46952.
\p
\v 12 “\add ≈Similarly,\add* if¦46956 the offering is¦46957 a¦46957 \bd goat¦46957\bd*, then¦46959 it¦46959 can be presented to¦46960 Yahweh¦46961.
\v 13 \add @The¦46963 presenter¦46963\add* will¦46963 put his¦46966 hand¦46966 on¦46967 its¦46969 head¦46969, and¦46970 slaughter it¦46971 \add ≈in¦46972 front¦46972\add* of¦46972 the¦46973 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦46973. Then¦46975 Aharon's¦46977 sons¦46976 must¦46975 splash¦46975 its¦46980 blood¦46980 on¦46981 the¦46983 altar¦46983, \add ≈on each¦46984 side\add*.
\v 14 From¦46987 that peace offering¦46989, he¦46986 must¦46986 present the fat as a¦46989 gift to¦46990 Yahweh¦46990, \add ≈along with\add* the¦46993 fat¦46993 covering¦46994 the¦46997 innards¦46997 and¦46998 which¦47002 is¦47003 part of the¦47005 innards¦47005,
\v 15 \add ≈both¦47008\add* kidneys¦47009 and¦47010 the¦47012 fat¦47012 that's¦47013 attached to them¦47014, and¦47019 the¦47021 lobe¦47021 on¦47022 the¦47024 liver¦47024 (all of which need to be removed¦47028 \add from the animal\add*).
\v 16 Then¦47030 the¦47031 priest¦47031 must burn¦47030 them on the¦47032 altar¦47032 as a food¦47033 offering¦47034 made¦47030 to¦47035 Yahweh by fire¦47034 as a pleasing¦47036 aroma¦47035. All¦47037 the fat¦47039 \add ≈belongs to¦47040\add* Yahweh¦47040.
