\v 17 “\add This\add* regulation¦47042 must be permanent¦47043 for \add all\add* \add ≈future\add* generations¦47044: All¦47045 of¦47045 you¦47054 must¦47054 \add ≈never\add* eat¦47054 fat¦47049 or blood¦47052.”
\c 4
\s1 Procedures for sin offerings
\rem /s1 Procedures for the Sin Offering; Offerings for Unintentional Sins; Sin Offerings; The Sin Offering
\p
\v 1 Then¦47057 Yahweh¦47058 told¦47057 Mosheh¦47061 \add !(Moses¦47061)\add*,
\v 2 “Tell¦47064 the¦47067 \add ≈Israelis¦47068\add* that if¦47072 a person¦47067 \add ≈breaks\add* any¦47083 of¦47077 Yahweh's¦47078 regulations \add ≈unintentionally¦47075\add*, or does anything that¦47079 he said¦47070 shouldn't¦47080 be¦47081 done¦47081, \add then this is the procedure:\add*
\p
\v 3 “If¦47086 it's \bd the¦47087 \+add ≈high\+add* priest¦47087\bd* \add ≈who's done it\add*, \add that causes\add* the¦47088 \add ≈nation\add* to¦47090 be guilty¦47090, and¦47092 for his transgression he¦47092 must¦47092 present¦47092 a¦47097 bull¦47097 \add ≈with no¦47101 defects¦47101\add* to¦47102 Yahweh¦47102 as a¦47103 sin¦47103 offering¦47103.
\v 4 He¦47105 must¦47105 bring¦47105 the¦47108 bull¦47108 before Yahweh at the¦47111 entrance¦47111 of¦47111 the¦47112 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦47112, then¦47116 he¦47116 must¦47116 place his¦47119 hand¦47119 on¦47120 \add *its\add* head¦47122 and¦47124 slaughter \add *it\add* \add ≈in¦47128 front¦47128\add* of¦47128 Yahweh¦47129.
\v 5 Then¦47131 the¦47132 \add ≈high\add* priest¦47132 must¦47131 get¦47131 some¦47134 of¦47134 the¦47135 bull's¦47135 blood¦47134 and¦47136 bringing¦47136 it¦47137 into¦47138 the¦47140 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦47140,
\v 6 he¦47143 must¦47143 dip¦47143 his¦47147 finger¦47147 into¦47148 \add *it\add* and¦47149 seven¦47153 times¦47154 he¦47149 must¦47149 \add ≈flick\add* the¦47152 blood¦47152 \add ≈towards\add* the¦47155 \add ≈front¦47155\add* of¦47159 the¦47160 curtain¦47160 of¦47160 the¦47161 sanctuary¦47161 \add ≈in¦47155 front¦47155\add* of¦47155 Yahweh¦47156.
\v 7 Then¦47163 the¦47164 \add high\add* priest¦47164 must put some¦47165 of¦47165 the¦47167 blood¦47167 on¦47168 the \add four\add* \add ≈projecting corners\add* of the incense altar (\add ≈located\add* inside the \add sacred\add* tent \add ≈in¦47174 front¦47174\add* of¦47174 Yahweh¦47175 \add and\add* used for \add burning\add* fragrant¦47173 incense). Then¦47179 \add he must go back outside and\add* pour¦47185 \add ≈the¦47183 rest\add* of¦47183 the¦47184 bull's¦47184 blood out¦47185 at the¦47188 base¦47188 of¦47188 the¦47189 altar¦47189 for burnt¦47190 \add #offerings¦47190\add* (which¦47191 is¦47193 \add out\add* at the¦47193 entrance¦47193 to the¦47194 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦47194).
\v 8 Then¦47197 \add @the high priest\add* must¦47204 \add ≈remove¦47204\add* all¦47199 the¦47201 fat¦47201 from the¦47202 bull¦47202 being offered as a sin¦47203 offering¦47203, \add including\add* the¦47208 fat¦47208 covering¦47209 the¦47212 innards¦47212 and¦47213 which¦47217 is¦47218 a part of the¦47220 innards¦47220,
\v 9 \add ≈both¦47223\add* kidneys¦47224 and¦47225 the¦47227 fat¦47227 that's¦47228 attached to them¦47229, and¦47234 the¦47236 lobe¦47236 on¦47237 the¦47239 liver¦47239 (all of which need to be removed¦47243 \add from the animal\add*)
\v 10 just¦47245 \add ≈like¦47245 you'd do\add* for the¦47247 bull¦47247 of the¦47249 peace¦47249 offering¦47249. Then¦47250 the¦47251 priest¦47251 must burn them on¦47252 the¦47253 altar¦47253 for the¦47254 burnt¦47254 offering¦47254.
\v 11 \add ≈However,\add* the¦47259 bull's¦47259 hide¦47258 and¦47260 its meat¦47264, plus its¦47267 head¦47267 and¦47268 feet, and¦47271 innards¦47271 and¦47272 dung¦47272,
\v 12 must¦47274 be taken outside¦47274 the camp¦47283 to¦47284 the clean¦47287 place¦47286 where they pour¦47290 out¦47290 the¦47291 ashes¦47291, and¦47292 they must¦47292 \add make\add* a fire¦47297 with wood¦47296 there on top of¦47300 the¦47301 ashes¦47301 and burn¦47292 it¦47302 there.
\p
\v 13 “If¦47305 it's¦47311 the \bd whole¦47317 community\bd* that¦47321 \add unintentionally\add* transgresses by doing¦47324 something that Yahweh¦47320 prohibited, then¦47325 they'll¦47325 be¦47325 guilty¦47325 even if the community didn't¦47322 \add actually\add* notice.\x + \xo 4:13-21: \xt Num 15:22-26.\x*
\v 14 \add ≈When¦47327\add* they \add ≈become aware\add* of \add ≈what they've¦47330 done¦47327 wrong\add*, then the¦47328 community must¦47332 present¦47332 a¦47335 \add ≈young¦47335\add* bull¦47334 \add ≈in¦47341 front¦47341\add* of¦47341 the¦47342 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦47342 as a sin offering¦47338.
\v 15 Then¦47345 the¦47346 community¦47347 elders¦47346 must place their¦47350 hands¦47350 of¦47350 the¦47353 bull's head¦47353 \add ≈in¦47355 front¦47355\add* of¦47355 Yahweh¦47356, and¦47357 slaughter \add *it¦47362 there¦47362\add*.
\v 16 The¦47365 \add ≈high\add* priest¦47365 must¦47364 take¦47364 some¦47367 of¦47367 the¦47368 bull's¦47368 blood¦47367 into¦47369 the¦47371 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦47371
\v 17 and¦47374 seven¦47381 times¦47382 \add *he\add* must¦47374 dip¦47374 his¦47376 finger¦47376 in it and \add ≈flick\add* the¦47379 blood¦47379 \add ≈towards\add* the¦47383 \add ≈front¦47383\add* of¦47386 the¦47387 curtain¦47387 of the sanctuary \add ≈in¦47383 front¦47383\add* of¦47383 Yahweh¦47384.
\v 18 Then¦47389 he¦47392 must¦47392 put¦47392 some of the blood on¦47394 the¦47396 \add four\add* \add ≈projecting corners\add* of¦47396 the¦47397 \add incense\add* altar¦47397 (\add ≈located\add* inside the¦47399 \add sacred\add* tent \add ≈in¦47399 front¦47399\add* of¦47399 Yahweh¦47400). Then¦47404 \add he must go back outside and\add* pour¦47408 \add ≈the¦47402 rest of\add* the¦47407 bull's blood¦47407 out¦47408 at the¦47411 base¦47411 of¦47411 the¦47412 altar¦47412 for burnt¦47413 \add #offerings¦47413\add* (which¦47414 is¦47416 \add out\add* at the¦47416 entrance¦47416 to the¦47417 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦47417).
\v 19 Then¦47420 he¦47424 must¦47424 \add ≈remove¦47424\add* all¦47421 the fat¦47423 from¦47425 \add @the¦47425 slaughtered¦47425 bull¦47425\add* and¦47426 burn¦47426 up \add @that¦47426 fat¦47426\add* on the¦47427 altar¦47427,
\v 20 and¦47429 he¦47429 should process the bull¦47430 just¦47431 the same as¦47431 for a sin¦47434 offering¦47434. Then¦47439 the¦47441 priest¦47441 \add ≈will¦47439 have made¦47439 them¦47440 right with God\add* and¦47442 they'll be¦47442 forgiven¦47442.
\v 21 Then¦47445 he¦47445 must¦47445 take¦47445 \add the remaining parts of\add* the¦47448 bull¦47448 outside¦47451 the camp¦47452 and¦47453 burn¦47453 it¦47454 \add ≈as¦47455 described above\add* \add and\add* it will be¦47460 the¦47460 sin¦47460 offering¦47460 for the¦47461 community.
\p
\v 22 “If it's \bd a¦47466 leader¦47466\bd* that¦47475 \add ≈unintentionally¦47479\add* transgresses¦47467 by doing¦47468 something that his¦47474 god¦47474 Yahweh¦47473 prohibited, then¦47480 he'll¦47480 be¦47480 guilty¦47480.
\v 23 \add Alternatively, maybe someone else will point out his failing\add* to¦47485 him¦47485. Then¦47490 he¦47490 must¦47490 bring¦47490 an offering¦47493 of¦47493 a¦47494 male¦47494 goat¦47494 \add ≈with no¦47497 defects¦47497\add*.
\v 24 He¦47499 must¦47499 place his¦47500 hand¦47500 on¦47501 \add *its\add* head¦47503 and¦47505 slaughter it¦47506 in¦47507 the¦47507 place¦47507 where¦47508 \add the animals for\add* the¦47513 burnt¦47513 offering¦47513 are slaughtered. It will be a¦47516 sin¦47516 offering¦47516,
\v 25 and¦47519 the¦47520 priest¦47520 must¦47519 take¦47519 some¦47521 of¦47521 the¦47521 blood¦47521 of¦47521 that sin¦47522 offering¦47522 and with his¦47523 finger¦47523, put some of the blood¦47532 on the¦47536 \add four\add* \add ≈projecting corners\add* of¦47536 the¦47537 altar¦47537 for burnt¦47538 offerings¦47538.
\v 26 He¦47545 must¦47545 burn¦47545 up all¦47542 the fat¦47544 on the¦47546 altar¦47546 just like¦47547 the¦47547 fat¦47547 from the¦47549 peace¦47549 offering¦47549, and \add that way\add*, the¦47552 priest¦47552 will make \add @that¦47553 leader¦47553\add* \add ≈right with God\add* and¦47554 he'll¦47550 be¦47554 forgiven¦47554.
\p
\v 27 “If¦47558 it's \bd an \+add ordinary\+add* person¦47560\bd* who \add ≈unintentionally¦47563\add* transgresses¦47562 by¦47563 doing¦47566 something that¦47570 Yahweh¦47569 prohibited, then they'll¦47573 be¦47574 guilty¦47574.\x + \xo 4:27-31: \xt Num 15:27-28.\x*
\v 28 \add Alternatively, maybe someone else will point out their failing\add* to¦47578 them. Then¦47582 due to their transgression, \add @that¦47582 person¦47582\add* must¦47582 bring¦47582 an offering¦47583 of¦47583 a¦47584 female¦47584 goat¦47584 \add ≈with no¦47586 defects¦47586\add*.
\v 29 He¦47594 must¦47594 place his¦47597 hand¦47597 on¦47598 the¦47599 head¦47599 of¦47599 the¦47600 \add goat that's a\add* sin¦47600 offering¦47600, and¦47601 slaughter \add *it\add* at the¦47605 place¦47605 for burnt¦47606 offerings¦47606.
\v 30 Then¦47608 the¦47609 priest¦47609 must¦47608 take¦47608 some¦47610 of¦47610 the blood¦47610 \add and\add* with his¦47611 finger¦47611, put some of¦47611 the blood on¦47613 the¦47615 \add four\add* \add ≈projecting corners\add* of¦47615 the¦47616 altar¦47616 for burnt¦47617 \add #offerings¦47617\add*, and¦47618 then pour¦47623 \add the rest of\add* the¦47626 blood at the¦47627 altar's¦47627 base¦47626.
\v 31 Then¦47629 \add @the presenter\add* must pull out all¦47631 the fat¦47633 (just¦47635 like¦47635 it's¦47636 done for the¦47640 peace¦47640 offering¦47640), and¦47641 the¦47642 priest¦47642 will¦47641 \add ≈burn¦47641\add* it on the¦47643 altar¦47643 to¦47644 make a pleasing¦47645 aroma¦47644 for¦47646 Yahweh¦47646, and¦47647 to \add ≈make¦47647 that person right with God\add*, and¦47650 they'll be¦47650 forgiven¦47650.
\p
\v 32 “\add ≈But¦47654\add* if¦47654 it's a¦47656 lamb¦47656 that \add @the individual\add* wants to¦47659 bring as their sin¦47659 offering¦47659, then it must be a¦47660 female¦47660 \add ≈with no¦47661 defects¦47661\add*.
\v 33 \add @The¦47664 presenter¦47664\add* must¦47664 put their hand¦47667 on¦47668 the¦47669 head¦47669 of¦47669 the¦47670 \add ≈lamb\add* and¦47671 slaughter it¦47672 as a¦47673 sin¦47673 offering¦47673 at the¦47674 place¦47674 where¦47675 burnt¦47679 offerings¦47679 are slaughtered.
\v 34 Then¦47681 the¦47682 priest¦47682 must¦47681 take¦47681 some¦47683 of¦47683 the¦47683 blood¦47683 \add and\add* with his¦47685 finger¦47685, put some of¦47685 the blood on¦47687 the¦47689 \add four\add* \add ≈projecting corners\add* of¦47689 the¦47690 altar¦47690 for burnt¦47691 offerings¦47691, and¦47692 then pour¦47697 \add the rest of\add* the¦47700 blood at the¦47701 altar's¦47701 base¦47700.
\v 35 Then¦47703 \add @the presenter\add* must pull out all¦47705 the fat¦47707 (just¦47709 like¦47709 it's¦47710 done for the¦47715 peace¦47715 offering¦47715), and¦47716 the¦47717 priest¦47717 will¦47716 \add ≈burn¦47716\add* it on the¦47719 altar¦47719 to make a pleasing aroma for Yahweh¦47722, and¦47723 to \add ≈make¦47723 that¦47729 person right with God\add*, and¦47732 they'll be¦47732 forgiven¦47732.
\c 5
\s1 More needs for sin offerings
\rem /s1 Cases Requiring Sin Offerings; Sins Requiring a Sin Offering
\p
\v 1 “If¦47737 someone¦47736 is¦47744 a¦47744 witness¦47744 to a case \add ≈because of something they saw¦47746 or¦47747 knew¦47748 about\add*, and¦47753 hears¦47740 an¦47742 oath¦47742 \add in court\add* but doesn't \add ≈testify\add*, then they'll \add ≈become guilty¦47754\add*.
\p
\v 2 “If someone¦47757 touches¦47759 anything ‘unclean¦47763’ (e.g., a¦47765 dead domestic or¦47768 wild animal¦47771, or¦47773 some creature) \add ≈without realising it\add*, they \add still\add* become ‘unclean¦47780’ and¦47781 is¦47781 guilty¦47781.
\p
\v 3 “If¦47784 someone touches¦47785 anything ‘unclean¦47791’ from¦47794 \add another\add* person, even if they \add initially\add* \add ^didn't realise\add* \add ≈what it¦47794 was¦47797\add*, they become guilty¦47797.
\p
\v 4 “If¦47801 someone¦47820 makes a rash promise, whether it's¦47802 to do something good¦47808 or something bad, and¦47814 even if they were¦47814 \add just\add* speaking¦47803 carelessly but \add ≈find out\add* \add later\add*, they become guilty¦47819.
\p
\v 5 “\add ≈So¦47823 then¦47829\add* \add @the person\add* that¦47830 became guilty¦47826 from¦47828 any of the above, must¦47829 confess¦47829 their wrongdoing
\v 6 and¦47834 present a penalty to¦47838 Yahweh¦47838 to address that¦47841 wrongdoing, and must present a¦47843 female¦47843 lamb¦47847 or¦47848 young goat¦47850 as a¦47852 sin¦47852 offering¦47852, and¦47853 the¦47855 priest¦47855 will \add act on their behalf\add* \add ≈to make¦47853 them right with God\add*.
\p
\v 7 “\add ≈However if¦47858 that¦47870 person can't¦47860 afford\add* a¦47865 sheep¦47865, then¦47866 for their guilt¦47869 offering¦47869 because of¦47869 \add ≈their transgression\add*, they must bring¦47866 two¦47872 doves¦47879 or¦47874 \add ≈young¦47877\add* pigeons to¦47880 Yahweh¦47880—one¦47881 for a¦47882 sin¦47882 offering¦47882 and¦47883 one¦47883 for a¦47884 burnt¦47884 offering¦47884.
\v 8 \add @The¦47886 presenter¦47886\add* must¦47886 take¦47886 them¦47887 to¦47888 the¦47890 priest¦47890 who will¦47891 present¦47891 the¦47894 sin offering¦47895 first¦47896—twisting \add @the bird's\add* head¦47900 off¦47897 from¦47901 the neck¦47902, \add ≈but¦47903\add* not¦47903 \add ≈pulling\add* the body \add in half\add*.
\v 9 Then¦47906 he¦47906 must¦47906 sprinkle¦47906 some¦47907 of¦47907 the¦47907 blood¦47907 from that sin¦47908 offering¦47908 onto the¦47911 side¦47911 of¦47911 the¦47912 altar¦47912, and¦47913 then drain¦47915 out¦47915 the¦47918 rest¦47913 of¦47918 the blood at the¦47919 altar's¦47919 base¦47918. That will be¦47920 the sin¦47920 offering¦47920.
\v 10 The¦47925 second¦47925 \add >bird\add* will¦47926 be for a¦47927 burnt¦47927 offering¦47927 as per the¦47928 regulation¦47928. The¦47931 priest¦47931 will make¦47929 \add @the presenter\add* \add ≈right with God\add* after their wrongdoing, and¦47936 they'll be¦47936 forgiven¦47936.
\p
\v 11 “\add ≈However if¦47940 that¦47956 person still can't¦47942 afford\add* those two¦47945 doves¦47951 or¦47947 \add ≈young¦47949\add* pigeons, then¦47952 they can present¦47955 a kilogram of fine¦47960 wheat flour¦47960 for a¦47961 sin¦47961 offering¦47961. It mustn't have oil¦47966 or frankincense¦47971 in it because¦47972 it's a¦47973 sin¦47973 offering¦47973.
\v 12 \add @The¦47976 presenter¦47976\add* must¦47976 take¦47976 it¦47976 to¦47977 the¦47979 priest¦47979 who will¦47980 then take¦47980 a¦47980 handful of it, and¦47989 burn¦47989 that memorial¦47988 portion on the¦47990 altar¦47990 for burnt¦47992 offerings¦47992 to Yahweh¦47993. That will be¦47994 the sin¦47994 offering¦47994.
\v 13 The priest will¦47997 make¦47997 \add @the presenter\add* \add ≈right with God\add* after their wrongdoing as per one¦48006 of the above¦47998, and¦48008 they'll be¦48008 forgiven¦48008. \add The rest of\add* \add @the flour\add* will¦48010 be for the priest¦48011, similar¦48012 to a grain offering¦48012.”
\s1 More on guilt offerings
\rem /s1 Repayment Offerings; The Guilt Offering; Procedures for the Guilt Offering; Offerings with Restitution
\p
\v 14 Then¦48015 Yahweh¦48016 told¦48015 Mosheh¦48019 \add !(Moses¦48019)\add*,
\v 15 “If¦48023 someone¦48022 acts¦48025 unfaithfully¦48025 \add ≈but¦48027\add* \add ≈unintentionally¦48028\add* \add ≈desecrates something that's sacred¦48029\add* to Yahweh¦48030, then¦48031 because of¦48034 their guilt, \add @that person\add* must present ram¦48036 \add ≈with no¦48037 defects¦48037\add* from¦48038 the¦48040 flock¦48040, or silver¦48042 \add ≈coins using the official valuation¦48041\add*, as a¦48048 guilt¦48048 offering¦48048.
\v 16 They must also¦48050 compensate for the¦48055 sacred¦48055 item, but¦48057 with an extra twenty¦48059 percent¦48060. That must all be given¦48062 to¦48064 the¦48065 priest¦48065 who will¦48066 make¦48066 \add @the¦48067 presenter¦48067\add* \add ≈right with God\add* with that ram¦48068 as the¦48069 guilt¦48069 offering¦48069, and¦48070 they'll be¦48070 forgiven¦48070.
\p
\v 17 “If¦48074 someone¦48076 transgresses¦48078 by violating \add even\add* one¦48080 of¦48083 Yahweh's¦48084 \add ≈regulations or prohibitions\add*, even if they¦48087 didn't¦48088 realise¦48090 it, they become guilty¦48091 and¦48092 must¦48092 bear¦48092 responsibility for that¦48085 guilt¦48093.
\v 18 Then¦48095 \add @that¦48095 person¦48095\add* must¦48095 take¦48095 a¦48096 ram¦48096 from¦48098 the¦48100 flock¦48100 that \add ≈has no¦48097 defects¦48097\add* to¦48102 the priest for a¦48102 guilt¦48102 offering¦48102. Then the¦48105 priest¦48105 will¦48106 make¦48106 \add @the¦48107 presenter¦48107\add* \add ≈right with God\add* after that transgression (even if they weren't aware of¦48110 it), and they'll be¦48118 forgiven¦48118.
\v 19 That's a¦48121 guilt¦48121 offering¦48121, because they were clearly guilty before Yahweh¦48125.”
\c 6
\rem /s1 Sins Requiring a Guilt Offering
\p
\v 1 Then¦48129 Yahweh¦48130 told¦48129 Mosheh¦48133 \add !(Moses¦48133)\add*,
\v 2 “Someone¦48137 who transgresses¦48139 against¦48142 Yahweh¦48142 by \add ≈cheating\add* with respect to a¦48145 deposit¦48145 or¦48146 a¦48149 pledge, or¦48150 by theft¦48151 or¦48152 extortion,
\v 3 or¦48159 by finding¦48161 lost¦48162 property and¦48163 then denying¦48163 it¦48164, or making an¦48165 oath¦48165 that was knowingly false¦48168, or by any other typical transgression that¦48173 people¦48176 do¦48175,
\v 4 then they've become guilty¦48185 as a result of that transgression. \add @That¦48186 person¦48186\add* must¦48186 return¦48186 what was stolen or¦48192 extorted¦48197, or¦48198 \add ≡return¦48186\add* the¦48201 deposit¦48201 or¦48205 the¦48208 lost¦48208 property,
\v 5 or¦48213 \add ≈make amends for a false¦48219 oath¦48217\add*. They must¦48220 return¦48220 the full value plus¦48223 an extra twenty percent¦48224\x + \xo 6:5: \xt Num 5:5-8.\x* \add ≈as soon as the¦48226 guilt¦48231 is discovered\add*.
\v 6 Then¦48234 \add @that person\add* must¦48237 take¦48237 a¦48239 ram¦48239 from¦48241 the¦48243 flock¦48243 \add ≈with no¦48240 defects¦48240\add* to¦48245 the¦48248 priest¦48248 as a¦48245 guilt¦48245 offering¦48245 to¦48246 Yahweh¦48238,
\v 7 and¦48251 the¦48253 priest¦48253 will¦48251 make¦48251 \add @the¦48252 presenter¦48252\add* \add ≈right with Yahweh¦48255\add* after whatever that¦48262 transgression was to¦48265 make them guilty¦48265, and¦48256 they'll be¦48256 forgiven¦48256.
\s1 The fire and the ashes
\rem /s1 Further Instructions for the Burnt Offering; Sacrifices Burned Whole; The Burnt Offering; Instructions concerning Sacrifices
\p
\v 8 Then¦48270 Yahweh¦48271 told¦48270 Mosheh¦48274,
\v 9 “Tell¦48285 Aharon¦48281 \add !(Aaron¦48281)\add* and¦48282 his¦48284 sons¦48284 that¦48286 these are¦48287 the¦48287 \add #regulations\add* for the¦48288 burnt¦48288 \add #offerings¦48288\add*: The¦48290 burnt¦48290 offering¦48290 must¦48291 remain on¦48291 the¦48292 altar's hearth¦48292, on¦48293 the¦48295 altar¦48295 all¦48296 night¦48298 until¦48299 the¦48301 morning¦48301 and¦48302 the¦48302 fire¦48302 \add ≈must¦48304 be kept burning¦48304\add* on¦48305 it¦48305.
\v 10 Then¦48308 the¦48309 priest¦48309 must¦48308 \add ≈put¦48308 on¦48308\add* his¦48310 linen¦48311 underwear¦48312 and¦48312 linen¦48314 robe¦48310 and¦48319 \add ≈remove¦48319\add* the¦48322 fatty¦48322 \add #ashes¦48322\add* from the¦48328 burnt¦48328 \add #offerings¦48328\add* on¦48329 the¦48331 altar¦48331, and¦48332 pile¦48332 them beside¦48333 \add *it\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈After that\add*, he'll¦48337 \add ≈get changed again into his¦48340 regular\add* clothes¦48342 and¦48344 take¦48344 \add &those¦48347\add* \add #ashes¦48347\add* outside¦48350 the camp¦48351 to¦48352 a ‘clean¦48355’ place¦48354.
\v 12 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* the¦48358 fire¦48358 on¦48359 the¦48361 altar¦48361 must¦48362 be kept burning¦48362—it must never go out. Every morning the¦48369 priest¦48369 must put more wood¦48370 on the fire, then¦48373 he¦48373 must¦48373 arrange¦48373 more offerings on¦48374 the¦48375 fire¦48375—he¦48376 should burn¦48376 the¦48378 fat¦48378 of¦48378 the¦48379 fellowship offerings¦48379 on that fire so the smoke¦48376 rises.
\v 13 \add Yes,\add* the fire¦48382 must¦48384 burn¦48384 continually¦48383 on¦48385 the¦48387 altar¦48387—never going out.
\s1 Procedures for the grain offering
\rem /s1 Further Instructions for the Grain Offering; The Grain Offering; Grain Offerings
\p
\v 14 “Here's the¦48395 regulations for the¦48396 grain¦48396 offering¦48396: Aharon's¦48401 sons¦48399 must¦48397 present¦48397 it¦48398 \add ≈before¦48402\add* Yahweh¦48403 \add ≈in front¦48406\add* of¦48406 the¦48407 altar¦48407.
\v 15 \add @The¦48410 priest¦48410\add* must¦48410 take a handful¦48412 of¦48412 the¦48413 flour¦48413 from that¦48420 grain¦48414 offering¦48414, being sure it includes some¦48415 of¦48415 the oil¦48415 and¦48416 the incense, and¦48424 burn¦48424 it on the¦48425 altar¦48425 as a memorial¦48428 portion to become a pleasing¦48427 aroma¦48426 for¦48429 Yahweh¦48429.
\v 16 The¦48432 remainder¦48432 \add of that flour\add* will be \add ≈used as food\add* for Aharon¦48435 and¦48436 his¦48436 sons¦48436—they¦48434 must¦48434 eat¦48434 the flat¦48437 bread¦48437 in¦48439 a¦48439 sacred place¦48439, i.e., in¦48441 the¦48441 courtyard¦48441 of¦48441 the¦48442 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦48442.
\v 17 It¦48449 must¦48449 not¦48448 be¦48449 baked¦48449 with any rising agent. I¦48452 give¦48452 that to them from¦48454 \add ≈what's given to me\add*. It's¦48457 \add ≈very\add* sacred just like¦48458 the sin offering¦48458 and¦48459 the guilt offering¦48459.
\v 18 Any of¦48462 Aharon's¦48466 male¦48464 descendants¦48465 can eat¦48467 it¦48467—it'll be their portion¦48468 from¦48472 Yahweh's¦48473 gifts throughout the generations¦48471. Anyone who¦48475 touches¦48477 \add @Yahweh's¦48478 gifts¦48478\add* will¦48479 become sacred¦48479 \add themself\add*.”
\s1 Procedures for the ordination offering
\rem /s1 Procedures for the Ordination Offering
\p
\v 19 Then¦48483 Yahweh¦48484 told¦48483 Mosheh¦48487,
\v 20 “On¦48499 the¦48492 day¦48499 when one of¦48492 Aharon's¦48493 male descendants¦48494 is consecrated \add as a priest\add*, this¦48491 is what he must¦48497 present¦48497 to¦48498 Yahweh¦48498: a continual¦48506 grain¦48505 offering¦48505 of a kilogram of fine¦48504 wheat flour¦48504—half¦48507 for the morning¦48508 and¦48509 half¦48509 for the evening¦48510.
\v 21 It must be mixed¦48518 with \add olive\add* oil then cooked with oil on a flat pan. It¦48519 must then be broken¦48520 into pieces¦48520 and presented¦48523 as a¦48521 grain¦48521 offering¦48521 to make¦48517 a pleasing¦48526 aroma¦48524 for¦48527 Yahweh¦48527.
\v 22 The¦48530 priest¦48530 who's next in¦48532 line to become \add ≈high\add* priest must¦48534 offer¦48534 it and it must be completely¦48540 burnt¦48541 for Yahweh¦48539. This is a permanent¦48538 regulation.
\v 23 Any grain¦48546 offering¦48546 by a¦48547 priest¦48547 must be completely¦48548 burnt—it¦48549 must¦48549 not¦48550 be¦48551 eaten¦48551.”
\s1 Procedures for the sin offering
\rem /s1 Sin Offerings; Further Instructions for the Sin Offering; The Sin Offering
\p
\v 24 Then¦48555 Yahweh¦48556 told¦48555 Mosheh¦48559,
\v 25 “Tell¦48563 Aharon¦48566 and¦48567 his¦48569 sons¦48569 that¦48571 these are¦48572 the¦48572 \add #regulations\add* for the¦48573 sin¦48573 \add #offerings¦48573\add*: The¦48579 sin¦48579 offering¦48579 must¦48578 be slaughtered \add ≈in¦48580 front¦48580\add* of¦48580 Yahweh¦48581 at the¦48574 place¦48574 where¦48575 the¦48577 burnt¦48577 \add #offerings¦48577\add* are¦48582 slaughtered. It's a¦48582 \add ≈very\add* sacred \add activity\add*.
\v 26 The¦48587 priest¦48587 who¦48588 offers the sin¦48588 offering¦48588 \add ≈must¦48590 be the one to eat¦48590 it¦48590\add*. It¦48593 must¦48593 be¦48593 eaten¦48593 in a sacred place¦48591, i.e., in¦48594 the¦48594 courtyard¦48594 of¦48594 the¦48595 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦48595.
\v 27 Everything that¦48600 touches¦48602 the \add animal's\add* body will¦48604 become sacred¦48604. Anyone who \add ≈gets the blood¦48607 on¦48608 their\add* clothes¦48610, must wash¦48614 them in¦48615 a¦48615 sacred place¦48615.
\v 28 Any clay¦48621 pot that¦48622 it's¦48623 been¦48623 boiled¦48623 in¦48625, must¦48626 then be¦48626 shattered¦48626, but¦48627 if¦48627 it's boiled in¦48629 a¦48629 bronze¦48630 pot, then¦48632 that must¦48632 be¦48632 scoured¦48632 and¦48633 rinsed¦48633 with¦48634 water¦48634.
\v 29 Any male¦48639 in the priests'¦48640 \add families\add* may eat¦48641 it¦48642—it's¦48645 \add ≈very\add* sacred.
\v 30 \add ≈However,\add* every¦48648 sin¦48650 offering¦48650 that¦48651 has its¦48653 blood¦48653 taken¦48652 inside the¦48656 \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦48656 to¦48658 make¦48658 \add ≈someone right with God\add*, then¦48648 that¦48651 \add meat\add* mustn't be¦48661 eaten¦48661—it¦48663 must¦48663 be¦48663 completely burnt¦48663 up.
\c 7
\s1 Procedures for the guilt offering
\rem /s1 Repayment Offerings; The Guilt Offering; Further Instructions for the Guilt Offering
\p
\v 1 “Then¦48666 these are¦48667 the¦48667 \add #regulations\add* for the¦48668 \add ≈very\add* sacred guilt¦48668 \add #offerings¦48668\add*:
\v 2 The¦48675 guilt¦48682 offering¦48678 must¦48679 be slaughtered at the¦48679 same place¦48673 as the¦48682 burnt¦48678 \add #offerings¦48682\add*, and¦48683 the blood¦48685 must¦48686 be splashed¦48686 on¦48687 \add ≈each¦48690 side of\add* the¦48689 altar¦48689.
\v 3 \add @The presenter\add* must¦48696 present¦48696 all¦48693 the¦48699 fat¦48699 \add including\add* the fatty tail¦48699, the¦48702 fat¦48702 covering¦48703 the¦48706 innards¦48706,
\v 4 \add ≈both¦48709\add* kidneys¦48710 and¦48711 the¦48713 fat¦48713 that's¦48714 attached to them¦48715, and¦48720 the¦48722 lobe¦48722 on¦48723 the¦48725 liver¦48725 (\add ≈all of which\add* need to be removed¦48729 \add from the animal\add*).
\v 5 Then¦48731 the¦48733 priest¦48733 must¦48731 burn¦48731 those¦48732 on the¦48734 altar¦48734 as a¦48735 guilt¦48737 offering¦48735 to¦48736 Yahweh¦48736.
\v 6 Any male¦48742 in the priests'¦48743 \add families\add* may eat¦48744 it¦48744—it's¦48747 \add ≈very\add* sacred.
\v 7 The regulations are the same for the guilt offering¦48752 as¦48753 for the sin offering—the¦48757 priest¦48757 who¦48758 \add ≈offers the guilt offering\add* \add ≈must¦48759 be the one¦48755 to¦48762 eat it\add*.
\p
\v 8 “Whenever a priest¦48765 presents¦48766 someone's burnt¦48769 offering¦48769, the¦48771 skin¦48771 of¦48771 the¦48772 animal that¦48773 was presented¦48774 belongs¦48777 to¦48775 that priest¦48775.
\v 9 Any grain¦48781 offering¦48781 that's¦48782 baked¦48783 in¦48784 an oven¦48784, or cooked¦48787 in¦48788 a pan¦48788 or on¦48789 a¦48791 griddle, will belong¦48792 to¦48792 the priest¦48792 who¦48793 presents¦48793 it.
\v 10 Any grain¦48800 offering¦48800 that's either dry¦48804 or mixed¦48801 with¦48803 oil¦48803, belongs¦48809 to¦48805 all¦48805 of¦48807 Aharon's¦48808 male descendants¦48807 \add ≈without any distinction\add*.
\s1 Procedures for the peace offering
\rem /s1 The Fellowship Offering; Further Instructions; Fellowship Offerings; Further Instructions for the Peace Offering
\p
\v 11 “Then¦48814 these are¦48815 the \add #regulations\add* for sacrificing¦48816 peace¦48817 offerings¦48817 to present¦48819 to¦48820 Yahweh¦48820:
\v 12 If¦48822 it's¦48826 presented¦48827 \add ≈from thankfulness\add*, then the¦48831 sacrifice¦48831 \add ≈must be accompanied by\add* thanksgiving¦48832 flat¦48834 bread¦48834 buns (\add made from flour\add* mixed¦48835 with¦48836 \add olive\add* oil¦48836), and¦48837 flat¦48838 biscuits¦48837 smeared¦48839 with¦48840 oil¦48840, and¦48841 buns \add made from\add* fine¦48841 wheat flour¦48841 mixed with¦48845 oil¦48845,
\v 13 \add ≈plus\add* risen bread¦48850 rolls. \add All that\add* must¦48852 accompany the¦48856 peace¦48858 offering¦48858 \add ≈from thankfulness¦48857\add*.
\v 14 Then¦48860 he¦48860 must¦48860 present¦48860 one¦48862 of each¦48863 \add kind of bread\add* as a¦48866 contribution¦48866 to¦48867 Yahweh¦48867. Those will¦48875 belong¦48875 to¦48868 the priest¦48868 who¦48869 splashes¦48869 the¦48872 blood¦48872 for the¦48873 peace¦48873 offerings¦48873.
\v 15 The¦48877 meat¦48877 of¦48877 the¦48878 thankfulness¦48879 sacrifice¦48878 of¦48878 those peace¦48880 offerings¦48880 must¦48883 be¦48883 eaten¦48883 the \add ≈same day¦48881 that it's offered—none of can be left¦48886\add* until¦48888 morning¦48890.
\v 16 \add ≈However,\add* if¦48892 the sacrificed offering is¦48894 a¦48894 vow¦48894 or¦48896 freewill¦48897 offering¦48897, then it¦48905 can be¦48905 eaten¦48905 that same day and¦48906 \add also\add* the¦48906 next¦48906 day¦48906,
