\v 1 Then¦51692 Yahweh¦51693 told¦51692 Mosheh¦51696 and¦51697 Aharon¦51699:
\p
\v 2 If¦51703 \add someone discovers\add* a raised area on¦51706 their skin¦51706, or a scab or a¦51714 bright¦51714 spot¦51714, and¦51715 it¦51715 seems like an infectious skin disease¦51720, then¦51721 \add @that¦51721 person¦51721\add* should be¦51721 taken¦51721 to¦51722 a priest¦51725 (Aharon¦51724 or¦51726 one¦51729 of¦51730 his¦51730 sons¦51730),
\v 3 and¦51733 the¦51734 priest¦51734 must¦51733 \add ≈examine¦51733\add* their skin¦51738. If the¦51741 hair¦51741 in¦51742 the infected \add spot\add* has¦51743 turned¦51743 white¦51745 and¦51746 the¦51747 infection appears to be¦51748 deeper under the¦51749 skin¦51749, then it's \add confirmed as\add* an infectious skin¦51752 disease¦51752 and¦51754 \add ≈so\add* the¦51755 priest¦51755 must¦51756 pronounce the person as ‘unclean¦51756’.
\v 4 \add However,\add* if¦51759 it's a¦51761 white spot¦51761 \add ≈that doesn't seem\add* to be¦51766 deep¦51766, and the hair¦51773 hasn't turned¦51776 white¦51777, then¦51778 the¦51779 priest¦51779 \add must order\add* the¦51782 person to be quarantined for seven¦51783 days¦51784.
\v 5 Then¦51786 on the¦51789 seventh¦51789 day¦51788, if the infection is still there but¦51790 hasn't spread¦51796, then¦51799 the¦51800 priest¦51800 \add must order\add* a further seven¦51801 days¦51802 of quarantine.
\v 6 After that next seven days¦51808, if the¦51809 infection has¦51812 faded and¦51814 not¦51814 spread¦51816, the¦51817 priest must¦51819 pronounce the¦51820 person as ‘clean’—it was¦51821 just a¦51821 \add ≈sore\add* so¦51823 the person must¦51823 wash¦51823 their clothes¦51824 and¦51825 then they'll be¦51825 ‘clean¦51825’.
\v 7 \add ≈However,\add* if¦51827 the spot does spread¦51829 across the¦51831 skin \em after¦51833\em* the priest has¦51834 pronounced \add @the¦51834 person¦51834\add* to¦51835 be ‘clean’, then¦51839 they must¦51839 \add ≈return\add* to¦51841 the¦51843 priest¦51843 a¦51840 second¦51840 time.
