\v 35 then¦53439 the homeowner must¦53439 go and¦53444 inform the priest¦53445 that something like¦53447 an infection has¦53448 appeared¦53448 in¦53450 their house¦53450.
\v 36 The¦53453 priest¦53453 must¦53454 order that everything be removed out of the¦53457 house¦53457 before¦53458 \add *he\add* comes¦53459 to¦53461 \add ≈inspect it\add* \add ≈so¦53465 that\add* it won't¦53465 all¦53467 be¦53466 pronounced as ‘unclean¦53466’. After¦53471 \add ≈that's done\add*, he'll¦53473 go¦53473 to¦53475 see¦53475 the¦53478 house¦53478
\v 37 and¦53480 \add ≈examine¦53480\add* the¦53483 growth. If the¦53485 growth is¦53486 greenish¦53489 or¦53490 reddish¦53491 and¦53492 seems more¦53494 than¦53494 surface deep¦53493,
\v 38 then¦53498 the¦53499 priest¦53499 must¦53498 leave¦53498 the¦53502 house¦53502 via the¦53505 \add main\add* entrance¦53505 and¦53507 quarantine the¦53510 house¦53510 for seven¦53511 days¦53512.
\v 39 On the¦53517 seventh¦53517 day¦53516, the¦53515 priest¦53515 must¦53518 return¦53514 and¦53519 \add ≈examine¦53519 it¦53520\add* \add again\add*, and if the growth has¦53520 spread¦53520 on the¦53523 house¦53523 walls¦53522,
\v 40 then¦53525 \add *he\add* must¦53525 order that¦53531 those infected stones¦53530 be¦53532 pulled out¦53527 of the¦53533 wall and¦53534 thrown¦53534 outside¦53538 the city¦53539 into¦53540 a¦53542 place¦53542 \add that's considered\add* ‘unclean¦53543’.
\v 41 Then¦53545 \add the homeowner\add* must¦53548 scrape¦53548 \add ≈all¦53550 the¦53554 plaster off¦53556 the¦53559 inside¦53549 walls\add* and¦53551 \add also\add* \add ≈dispose of¦53560 that¦53555\add* at \add &that¦53563\add* ‘unclean¦53564’ place¦53563.
\v 42 Then they \add ≈can replace the¦53573 stones¦53573 that were removed\add*, and \add ≈apply fresh plaster¦53577\add* to the¦53580 house¦53580.
\p
\v 43 \add ≈However,\add* if¦53582 the¦53585 growth returns¦53584 and¦53586 breaks¦53586 out¦53586 \add again\add* in¦53587 the house¦53587 \add even\add* after¦53588 \add ≈the¦53592 stones¦53592 were replaced and¦53593 the¦53597 walls were¦53599 replastered\add*,
\v 44 then¦53601 the¦53602 priest¦53602 must¦53603 come¦53601 \add back\add* and¦53604 \add ≈reexamine\add* it¦53605. If the growth has¦53605 spread¦53605 \add ≈on the¦53606 walls\add*, then it's a¦53608 malignant¦53609 growth and \add @the¦53610 house¦53610\add* is¦53612 ‘unclean¦53612’.
\v 45 \add @The¦53615 owner¦53615\add* must¦53615 tear¦53615 the¦53618 house¦53618 down¦53615—its¦53621 stones¦53621 and¦53622 timber¦53624 and¦53625 all¦53626 the mortar, must¦53630 be \add ≈carted\add* outside¦53630 the¦53633 city¦53634 into¦53635 a¦53637 place¦53637 \add that's considered\add* ‘unclean¦53638’.
