\v 16 \add ≈Now\add* when¦54058 a¦54058 man¦54058 has an \add ≈emission of¦54063 semen¦54065\add*, then¦54066 he¦54066 must¦54066 bathe his entire¦54070 body¦54072 in water¦54067, and¦54073 he'll¦54073 be¦54073 ‘unclean¦54073’ until¦54074 the¦54076 evening¦54076.
\v 17 He must also¦54078 wash¦54091 all¦54078 his clothing¦54080, and¦54081 any leather¦54083 articles on¦54087 him¦54087 \add ≈that¦54084 came into contact with¦54092 the semen¦54090\add* and¦54093 \add @all¦54093 of¦54093 that¦54093\add* will¦54093 be¦54093 ‘unclean¦54093’ until¦54094 the¦54096 evening¦54096.
\v 18 \add ≈When¦54099 a man¦54102 and a¦54104 woman¦54099 ‘sleep together’\add*, then¦54107 they¦54107 must¦54107 both bathe in water¦54108, and¦54109 they'll¦54109 \add both\add* be¦54109 ‘unclean¦54109’ until¦54110 the¦54112 evening¦54112.\f + \fr 15:18 \ft Note that if they had sexual relations in the evening, say 9pm, then they'd be ‘unclean’ all the next day and until the \+em following\+em* evening (because the Jewish ‘day’ begins after dusk—rather than at midnight like modern Western society counts time).\f*
\p
\v 19 When¦54114 a¦54114 woman¦54114 \add ≈has her menstrual period\add*, she'll¦54117 be ‘unclean’ for seven¦54123 days¦54124, and¦54127 anyone¦54129 who¦54129 touches¦54129 her¦54130 \add ≈during that time\add* will¦54131 be¦54131 ‘unclean¦54131’ until¦54132 the¦54134 evening¦54134.
