\v 3 Tell¦57342 them¦57343 that \add ≈throughout\add* the generations¦57344, any \add ≈of¦57344 your¦57344 descendants\add* who¦57349 is ‘\add ≈unclean¦57364\add*’ and approaches¦57351 things¦57357 that¦57358 have become holy¦57359 because the¦57360 people¦57360 have consecrated them to¦57363 Yahweh¦57363, \add @that person\add* will¦57366 be¦57366 cut¦57366 off¦57366 from¦57369 me¦57369. I¦57370 am¦57371 Yahweh¦57371.
\p
\v 4 Any man¦57373 who's a¦57374 descendant of Aharon¦57376, if he¦57377 has¦57378 a¦57378 skin¦57378 disease¦57378 or¦57379 a discharge¦57380, he¦57383 mustn't eat¦57383 any of the sacred \add >food\add* until¦57384 he's¦57386 ‘clean¦57386’ \add again\add*. \add ≈The¦57387 same applies if\add* he's touched¦57387 any ‘unclean¦57390’ corpse¦57392, anyone¦57394 who's¦57395 had a¦57399 seminal emission,
\v 5 anyone¦57405 who's¦57406 touched¦57407 any¦57421 swarming¦57410 \add >creature\add* that¦57411 makes him ‘unclean’ or¦57415 \add ≡touches\add* \add another\add* person who¦57417 makes him ‘unclean’ (whatever that person's uncleanness¦57422 is).
\v 6 \add No,\add* the man who's¦57425 touched¦57426 any of those will¦57429 be¦57429 ‘unclean¦57429’ until¦57430 the¦57432 evening¦57432 and¦57433 he¦57434 mustn't eat¦57434 any¦57435 of¦57435 the¦57437 sacred¦57437 \add >food\add* until he's¦57441 washed¦57441 his¦57442 body¦57442 with¦57443 water¦57443.
\v 7 When¦57445 the¦57446 sun¦57446 sets, then¦57447 he'll¦57447 be¦57447 ‘clean¦57447’ and¦57448 will¦57449 be able to eat¦57449 any¦57450 of¦57450 those sacred¦57452 \add >offerings\add* because¦57453 that's his¦57454 food¦57454.
\v 8 \add ≈But¦57458\add* he¦57460 must¦57460 \add ≈never\add* eat¦57460 \add ≈an animal¦57458 found dead\add* or torn¦57458 \add by wild animals\add* and become¦57461 ‘unclean¦57461’ \add ≈in that way\add*. I¦57464 am¦57465 Yahweh¦57465.
\p
