\v 22 not blind¦57690 or with broken \add bones\add*, and not maimed or with an oozing sore¦57698 or¦57699 rash¦57700 or¦57701 scab¦57702. You¦57705 all mustn't present¦57705 \add ≈anything like that\add* to¦57707 Yahweh¦57707, and¦57708 must not \add even\add* offering¦57708 \add ≈any part of them¦57712\add* to Yahweh on¦57713 the¦57715 altar¦57715.
\v 23 \add ≈However,\add* if a cow¦57718 or a¦57719 sheep¦57719 has¦57720 something¦57720 enlarged¦57720 or something¦57721 stunted¦57721, it can be offered as a¦57722 freewill¦57722 offering¦57722, but it¦57724 wouldn't be¦57727 accepted¦57727 for¦57725 a¦57725 vow¦57725,
\v 24 and you¦57734 all must¦57734 never present¦57734 to¦57735 Yahweh¦57735 any animal that's bruised or torn¦57731 or cut¦57732.\f + \fr 22:24 \ft The Septuagint mentions ‘testicles’ here, which also correlates with 21:20.\f* You mustn't do that in¦57736 your \add ≈country¦57736\add*.
\p
