\p
\v 27 A \add newborn\add* calf or lamb¦57773 or¦57774 goat¦57776 must¦57778 \add ≈remain with\add* its¦57783 mother¦57783 for seven¦57780 days¦57784—it¦57787 can be¦57787 offered¦57789 as a sacrifice¦57789 to¦57790 Yahweh¦57790 from the¦57785 eighth¦57785 day onwards¦57786,
\v 28 \add ≈but¦57792\add* you mustn't slaughter a cow¦57792 or¦57793 a¦57795 sheep¦57795 and its¦57796 \add ≈offspring\add* on¦57802 \add ≈the¦57801 same\add* day¦57802.
\v 29 When¦57805 you¦57807 \add ≈offer\add* a¦57808 thanksgiving¦57810 sacrifice to¦57811 Yahweh¦57811, it must be \add ≈acceptable¦57812 as a sacrifice¦57813\add*
\v 30 and you can eat¦57817 it that¦57816 same day¦57815 \add but\add* \add ≈no part\add* of it¦57817 should be¦57817 left¦57820 until¦57822 the morning¦57824. I¦57825 am¦57826 Yahweh¦57826.
\p
\v 31 You¦57828 all must¦57828 \add ≈record my¦57829 instructions¦57829 and¦57830 follow\add* them¦57831. I¦57832 am¦57833 Yahweh¦57833.
\v 32 You¦57836 mustn't profane¦57836 the¦57839 \add ≈reputation¦57839\add* of¦57839 my¦57840 holiness¦57840, and¦57841 I¦57841 will¦57841 demonstrate¦57841 my holiness¦57841 among the¦57842 Israeli¦57844 people¦57843. I¦57845 am¦57846 Yahweh¦57846 who¦57847 separates you¦57847 all to be sacred¦57847—
\v 33 who¦57849 brought¦57849 you all out¦57849 of¦57851 Egypt¦57852 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* to¦57853 be¦57853 your god¦57855. I¦57856 am¦57857 Yahweh¦57857.
