\v 5 The¦57920 14th of the¦57921 first¦57921 month¦57924 \add (Nisan = March/April) each year\add* \add ≈at twilight¦57926\add* is the¦57926 \add start of the celebration to honour\add* Yahweh¦57928 with the ‘passover¦57927’.\x + \xo 23:5: \xt Exo 12:1-13; Deu 16:1-2.\x*
\p
\v 6 Then¦57930 the¦57930 \add next day\add* (the¦57934 15th) is \add the start of\add* the¦57935 festival¦57935 of¦57935 flat¦57936 bread¦57936 \add to honour\add* Yahweh¦57937—you¦57941 all must¦57941 eat¦57941 bread made without any rising agent for seven¦57938 days¦57939.\x + \xo 23:6-8: \xt Exo 12:14-20; 23:15; 34:18; Deu 16:3-8.\x*
\v 7 On \add &that\add* first¦57944 day¦57943 you'll¦57955 hold a¦57945 \add ≈sacred¦57947\add* assembly¦57945—no \add ≈regular\add* work¦57952 may be done¦57955 \add that day\add*.
