\v 13 and¦58039 the \add associated\add* grain¦58039 offering¦58039 will¦58040 be¦58040 two¦58040 kilograms of¦58040 fine¦58042 wheat flour¦58042 mixed¦58043 with¦58044 \add olive\add* oil¦58044. That will be a¦58045 gift to¦58046 Yahweh¦58046 with a pleasing¦58048 aroma¦58047, and¦58049 the \add associated\add* drink¦58049 offering¦58049 will¦58051 be¦58051 a litre of wine¦58051.
\v 14 You all¦58074 may not eat¦58059 any bread¦58055, or roasted¦58056 or fresh grain¦58056, on that day¦58063, until¦58065 \add after\add* you've¦58066 taken the¦58069 offering¦58069 to your¦58070 god¦58070. That is a¦58071 \add ≈rule that will continue throughout\add* your¦58073 generations¦58073 \add ≈no matter where\add* you live¦58075.
