\v 16 Then that next¦58094 day¦58094 \add will make\add* fifty¦58098 days¦58099, and¦58100 then you¦58100 all must¦58100 present¦58100 a¦58101 new¦58102 grain¦58101 offering¦58101 to¦58103 Yahweh¦58103.
\v 17 From¦58105 your¦58105 \add ≈homes\add*, \add @each¦58106 family¦58106\add* must¦58106 bring¦58106 two loaves of¦58111 bread¦58108 baked¦58116 with a rising agent, as a firstfruits¦58117 \add offering\add* to¦58118 Yahweh¦58118.
\v 18 Along with¦58121 the¦58123 bread¦58123, you all must present¦58120 seven¦58124 \add ≈year-old\add* male¦58125 lambs¦58125 \add ≈without¦58126 defects¦58126\add*, one \add ≈young¦58127\add* bull¦58129, and¦58134 two¦58135 rams¦58134. They¦58136 will¦58136 be¦58136 a¦58137 burnt¦58137 offering¦58137 to¦58138 Yahweh¦58138, with their¦58139 \add associated\add* grain¦58139 and¦58140 drink¦58140 offerings¦58140—a gift with a pleasing¦58144 aroma¦58142 for¦58145 Yahweh¦58145.
\v 19 You¦58147 all must¦58147 \add also\add* offer¦58147 a¦58148 male¦58148 goat¦58148 as a¦58152 sin¦58152 offering¦58152 and¦58153 two¦58153 \add ≈one-year-old\add* male¦58154 lambs¦58154 as a peace¦58158 offering¦58158.
\v 20 The¦58161 priest¦58161 must raise them¦58163 along with¦58164 the¦58166 firstfruits¦58166 bread¦58165 as a¦58167 wave¦58160 offering \add ≈in¦58168 front¦58168\add* of¦58168 Yahweh¦58169, with¦58170 the two¦58172 lambs¦58173. They¦58175 will¦58175 become sacred¦58174 to¦58176 Yahweh¦58176, \add but\add* for¦58177 the priest¦58177 \add to eat\add*.
\v 21 You¦58179 all¦58197 must¦58179 proclaim¦58179 a¦58184 \add ≈sacred¦58186\add* assembly¦58184 that same day¦58182—you¦58188 mustn't do any¦58189 \add ≈regular\add* work¦58191. That is a¦58195 \add ≈permanent¦58196\add* rule that will continue \add ≈throughout\add* the generations¦58200 \add ≈no matter where you live¦58199\add*.
\p
\v 22 When¦58202 you¦58202 all harvest¦58205 your \add ≈crops\add*, don't¦58207 \add ≈reap\add* to the¦58210 very edge of¦58210 your¦58211 field¦58211 and¦58213 don't \add ≈pick up stalks that drop on the¦58213 ground¦58206\add*—they must¦58216 be left¦58219 for¦58217 the poor and¦58218 for¦58218 foreigners¦58218 \add without land\add*.\x + \xo 23:22: \xt Lev 19:9-10; Deu 24:19-22.\x* I¦58221 am¦58222 your¦58223 god¦58223, Yahweh¦58222.
